% Test cases for the infrared heating pad policy (infrared_heating.le):
% synthetic claims for the system and its replacement pads. The policy
% concludes nothing — LCD L33825, applying NCD 270.6, denies the device and
% its accessories as not reasonable and necessary — so every claim fails at
% the question, however complete its documentation, and no change of the
% record makes one payable.

the target language is: prolog.

the knowledge base infrared_heating cases includes these resources:
    infrared_heating.

the knowledge base infrared_heating cases includes:

query pay is:
    which claim is payable.

query rn is:
    which claim is reasonable and necessary.

query stage is:
    the query fails at which section.

query flip is:
    which minimal change to the scenario makes it the case that
        claim 1 is payable.

% A fully documented claim for an infrared heating pad system (E0221) for
% chronic low back pain: denied all the same, and nothing flips it.
scenario system_complete is:
    claim 1 is for the infrared system.
    the HCPCS code of the infrared system is "E0221".
    the infrared system is furnished to Ann.
    the residence of Ann is private residence.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-03-01.
    the order for the infrared system is dated 2026-02-20.
    the order for the infrared system is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the infrared system includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the infrared system includes order date.
    the order for the infrared system includes description of the item.
    the order for the infrared system includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the infrared system includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the infrared system was communicated to the supplier on 2026-02-22.
    the infrared system was delivered on 2026-03-01.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for the infrared system.
    pay expects answers [].
    rn expects answers [].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at question"].
    flip expects changes [].

% A replacement pad (A4639) for a beneficiary-owned system: a supply of
% a device that is itself never covered.
scenario replacement_pad is:
    claim 1 is for the replacement pad.
    the HCPCS code of the replacement pad is "A4639".
    the replacement pad is furnished to Ben.
    the residence of Ben is private residence.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-03-01.
    the HCPCS code of the infrared system is "E0221".
    the infrared system is furnished to Ben.
    pay expects answers [].
    rn expects answers [].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at question"].

% A system furnished to a skilled nursing facility resident: not a home, so
% the claim fails already at applicability.
scenario system_in_nursing_facility is:
    claim 1 is for the infrared system.
    the HCPCS code of the infrared system is "E0221".
    the infrared system is furnished to Cy.
    the residence of Cy is skilled nursing facility.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-03-01.
    pay expects answers [].
    rn expects answers [].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at applicability"].

% An electric heating pad (E0210) is not this policy's: out of its scope
% (heating_pads.le decides it).
scenario electric_pad_out_of_scope is:
    claim 1 is for the heating pad.
    the HCPCS code of the heating pad is "E0210".
    the heating pad is furnished to Dee.
    the residence of Dee is private residence.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-03-01.
    pay expects answers [].
    rn expects answers [].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at applicability"].
